{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474114-art-forger-concept-build-help","id":1474114,"title":"Art Forger - Concept Build help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-07T02:49:50-08:00","id":1474114,"title":"Art Forger - Concept Build help","content":"Hello, <br /> recently i was thinking about the Art Forger archetype. <br /> Does anyone wanna help with building the character? <br /> What are your thoughts on somebody like that? <br /> Should he be a Daeva or something else, and why? <br /> How do you see that kind of character in a long run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T04:31:15-08:00","id":1474119,"title":"","content":"Well, from a clan perspective, i fail to see a reason (beside correlation with the Toreador bloodline) for a Daeva to be any more or less appropriate a choice for an Art Forger type of character.<br /> <br /> While the concept can evoke themes from Requiem - someone who lives from manipulating people into giving the fruit of their labors, knowingly or not, for what are forgeries, falsehoods, things whose value is in a facade - it doesn't resonate in and on itself with any one clan, be it Daeva, Gangrel, Mekhet, Nosferatu or Ventrue. Any of them or some of the alternate/lost clans might roll with with it, imho.<br /> <br /> I guess the major question is how that role would influence and/or define the character's requiem, how he or she leverages it into facilitating its undead existence or coloring the endless routine of unlife and maybe weaving &amp; reweaving the continually fraying threads of one's humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T11:40:09-08:00","id":1474138,"title":"","content":"Daeva aren't Toreador. Some of them certainly are into art, but as a clan, they're primarily fixated on people.<br /> <br /> <i>The Spirit's Touch</i> can change the way that vampires perceive any object depending on its history. Therefore, vampires with Auspex are able to appreciate original works of art in a way that mortals don't. So they might feel more entitled to the originals than mortals. Like minded vampires probably annoy their peers by dropping hints about the artist's experiences and then saying &quot;but you don't see as we do, you wouldn't understand&quot;.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, I can totally see Invictus hoarding art out of vanity or as an investment. They could even leak that the art in the gallery is forgery a few centuries later and encourage a worldwide hunt for the original for the hype before selling it somehow for vastly more than it was worth before anyone cared about it. The Invictus book has some ideas about patrons of art and guilds, so if you have a copy of that, it might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 02-07-2022, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T18:43:24-08:00","id":1474153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474114-art-forger-concept-build-help?p=1474138#post1474138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daeva aren't Toreador. Some of them certainly are into art, but as a clan, they're primarily fixated on people.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the Toreador were the sample Daeva bloodline in Requiem 1e, so i can't see people making a connection, ergo my own reaction to the OP's initial suggestion of Daeva.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474114-art-forger-concept-build-help?p=1474138#post1474138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Spirit's Touch</i> can change the way that vampires perceive any object depending on its history. Therefore, vampires with Auspex are able to appreciate original works of art in a way that mortals don't. So they might feel more entitled to the originals than mortals. Like minded vampires probably annoy their peers by dropping hints about the artist's experiences and then saying &quot;but you don't see as we do, you wouldn't understand&quot;.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, I can totally see Invictus hoarding art out of vanity or as an investment. They could even leak that the art in the gallery is forgery a few centuries later and encourage a worldwide hunt for the original for the hype before selling it somehow for vastly more than it was worth before anyone cared about it. The Invictus book has some ideas about patrons of art and guilds, so if you have a copy of that, it might help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. Mekhet Invictus, combining a bit of both angles in a whole, could make for an interesting sprinboard. It also goes quite well with the shadowy/underworld/criminal side of the art forgery endeavour proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-07-2022, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T18:50:17-08:00","id":1474154,"title":"","content":"A built-in conflict story hook I can see is an Elder barging into the young forger\u2019s \u2018office\u2019 and demanding compensation over how the forgeries have marred the value of the Elder\u2019s own exquisite art collection.<br /> <br /> Or maybe such an encounter has already happened, and serves as the background for some Social Merits and other in-universe connections the forger has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-07-2022, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T01:49:56-08:00","id":1474175,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, the Toreador clan from VtM does have Auspex, so if you're up for homebrewing an update of the Toreador bloodline from VtR you could just change Dominate to Auspex and go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:38:07-08:00","id":1474199,"title":"","content":"Hahaha. I created two characters who were art forgers. One was a Ventrue who liked to draw in her spare time and on a dare forged the signature of a regent granting temporary feeding privileges to a friend of a friend. Eventually escalating to where a few Sanctified and Invictus members (closer to elders than ancillae) discreetly approached her to create fake sketchbooks and unfinished paintings of various artists so they could claim they were soandso's anonymous patron.<br /> <br /> Another one was a Ventrue with college degrees in art history and composition and chemistry who started obsessing over the &quot;imperfections&quot; of &quot;near flawless&quot; works of art. She'd forge them, then &quot;perfect&quot; them. She managed to scam quite a few art collectors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}